# Newsletter & Resend

## Source of truth

- **Subscribers**: `newsletter_subscribers` in Supabase is authoritative (`is_active`, `unsubscribe_token`, consent via C-end form).
- **Resend**: delivery mirror only — sync contacts/segment on subscribe/unsubscribe; do not treat Resend Audience as the only subscriber list.
- **Templates**: `newsletter_templates` in DB; defaults/seeds in `@/lib/newsletter-email-templates.ts`. Admin edits HTML in portal; avoid a second template source in Resend Dashboard.

## Delivery stack

| Email type | API | Unsubscribe |
|------------|-----|-------------|
| Welcome / resubscribe / unsubscribe confirm | Resend `emails.send` (fallback SMTP) | Blaze `{{unsubscribe_link}}` → `/newsletter/unsubscribe?token=` |
| Marketing campaigns | Resend **Broadcast** when `RESEND_NEWSLETTER_SEGMENT_ID` set; else per-recipient `emails.send` | Broadcast: `{{{RESEND_UNSUBSCRIBE_URL}}}` in HTML; webhook must sync `contact.unsubscribed` to Blaze |

- Entry: `sendNewsletterEmail()` in `@/lib/email.ts` (Resend if `RESEND_API_KEY`, else Nodemailer).
- Render placeholders: `prepareNewsletterHtmlForSend()` in `@/lib/newsletter-template-runtime.ts`.
- Campaign send: `sendNewsletterCampaign()` in `@/lib/newsletter-campaign-send.ts` — do not reintroduce long inline `for` loops in route handlers.
- Contact sync: `syncSubscriberToResend()` in `@/lib/newsletter-resend-sync.ts` after subscribe/unsubscribe (non-blocking).

## Template placeholders (filled at send time)

- `{{unsubscribe_link}}` — per-subscriber token URL (required for transactional templates).
- `{{website_url}}`, `{{contact_email}}`, `{{body_content}}` — see `newsletter-email-templates.ts`.
- Do not hardcode final unsubscribe URLs in stored template HTML.

## Seeded template names (stable)

Use `NEWSLETTER_TEMPLATE_NAMES` from `@/lib/newsletter-email-templates.ts`:

- `Welcome — First Subscription`
- `Welcome — Resubscribe`
- `Unsubscribe Confirmation`
- `Latest Updates — Newsletter`

Seed/upsert: `npm run seed:newsletter-templates`.

## Public vs admin

- **Public**: `POST /api/public/newsletter/subscribe`, `GET /api/public/newsletter/unsubscribe`, Information Clause in `@/lib/newsletter-information-clause.ts`.
- **Admin** (`role === "admin"`): templates CRUD, campaigns, send/schedule, statistics, failed-sends; delivery status UI via `NewsletterDeliveryPanel` + `GET /api/admin/newsletter/delivery-config`.

## UI language

- User-facing copy under `src/app/**/newsletter/**` and `src/components/admin/newsletter/**` must be **English** (labels, toasts, errors, empty states, confirmations). Code comments may stay bilingual; do not ship Chinese UI strings on these pages.
- **Webhook**: `POST /api/webhooks/resend` — verify `RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (Svix headers); update `newsletter_sends` / deactivate subscriber on bounce or `contact.unsubscribed`.

## Env vars

- `RESEND_API_KEY`, `RESEND_NEWSLETTER_FROM` (or `RESEND_FROM`)
- `RESEND_NEWSLETTER_SEGMENT_ID` — enables Broadcast for bulk sends
- `RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` — unsubscribe link base

## Schema (Resend columns)

Run `sql/root-migrations/migrate-newsletter-resend.sql` if missing: `resend_contact_id`, `resend_broadcast_id`, `resend_email_id`.

## Do not

- Block subscribe API on welcome-email failure (send async; log errors).
- Assume Resend unsubscribe alone updates Blaze without webhook or Blaze token flow.
- Add new `.md` docs for this feature (use this rule + code comments for non-obvious logic).
- Mix franchise/catalog `product-hierarchy` terms into user-facing newsletter copy (brand: **Blaze Robotics Academy**, **BlazeRoboticsAcademy.org**).
